# The barrier the White Knight raises by shouting at enemies in front of them.
# enemy_attack_pct handles it: it weakens the mob before its hit is rolled, so
# the character's DEF then cancels a larger share of what is left.
#
# GMS also lowers the enemy's DEF and accuracy by the same share. Neither is
# modelled: this game doesn't lower a monster's DEF, and there is no accuracy.
#
# Its success rate is dropped, not averaged in. GMS runs the debuff for 40 + 2L
# seconds from a cast the player can repeat until it lands, so the rate costs
# casts, not damage, and the debuff is permanent here like every window that can
# simply be recast.
#
# Its six-enemy reach doesn't matter either: only the mob at the front of the
# queue attacks.
name: "Noble Demand"
description:
  "Releases the pride of the Holy Knight, decreasing the Attack Power of "
  "nearby enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_WHITE_KNIGHT skill_order: 3 }
max_level: 20
base { enemy_attack_pct: 0.30 }
per_level { enemy_attack_pct: 0.01 }
